[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1264383502","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651#issuecomment-1264383502","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651","id":1264383502,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85LXPYO","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-10-01T14:35:24Z","updated_at":"2022-10-01T14:35:24Z","body":"Proposed short name: Adobe-FreeType-Patent\r\n\r\nURL: See e.g. https://github.com/freetype/freetype/blob/master/src/psaux/psarrst.c\r\n\r\nThis license text appears on several source files in FreeType, which is packaged in Linux distributions like Fedora and widely used in commercial products. I assume Adobe provided this text in certain contributions it made to FreeType. It in a sense incorporates the FreeType license (SPDX: FTL) by reference and adds a patent license grant similar to Apache-2.0 section 3. \r\n\r\nI am aware of the [past issue](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/646) involving a variety of Google open source project patent license grant where SPDX-legal did not resolve whether language of this sort (an ancillary patent license grant supplementing the terms of a FOSS project license) would be appropriate for inclusion in the SPDX license list, and whether it is what SPDX considers an \"exception\". I note also that SPDX has left open an [issue ](https://github.com/spdx/spdx-spec/issues/153)from several years ago proposing that an equivalent to LicenseRef- be adopted specifically for exception-like constructs. I believe that SPDX should now address the unresolved questions raised in these issues. While Fedora could use something like LicenseRef-FTL-WITH-Adobe-FreeType-Patent to represent these terms, Fedora's policy is to request SPDX identifiers for all approved license language, and using a 'WITH' expression referencing a standard SPDX identifier inside a 'LicenseRef-' seems particularly undesirable.\r\n\r\nFedora priority: low. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1264383502/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1363394252","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651#issuecomment-1363394252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651","id":1363394252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85RQ77M","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-22T22:11:28Z","updated_at":"2022-12-22T22:11:28Z","body":"+1 to @richardfontana's comment [above](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651#issuecomment-1264383502), noting the similarity of this to the prior \"and here's a patent license\" texts.\r\n\r\nI think this is worth discussing and reaching some sort of conclusion on, whether it's to consider modifying how exceptions work generally, or else to determine how we'll handle these sort of modifiers when they are tagged onto another license.\r\n\r\nI'll mark this as needing discussion on an upcoming legal team call, though not sure whether this will be covered in the time remaining for 3.20.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1363394252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1603014385","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651#issuecomment-1603014385","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651","id":1603014385,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fjA7x","user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T16:59:28Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T16:59:28Z","body":"I do not think that this proposal aligns with #3 of the [License Exception rubric](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md#license-exceptions).  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1603014385/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1603398117","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651#issuecomment-1603398117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651","id":1603398117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fkenl","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T22:38:35Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T22:38:35Z","body":"discussed (again) on 6/22 call: looking more closely at this in light of our now articulated exception guidelines, we all agreed this doesn't not really meet those. Specifically it doesn't fit squarely in either of the two aspects of (2) and contains a restriction or limitation beyond those granted in the underlying license. It was also noted that these kinds of patent licenses seemed to have a period of popularity, but that has waned (in relation to substantial use).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1603398117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1603398788","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651#issuecomment-1603398788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1651","id":1603398788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fkeyE","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.g